A||||1||grinthock||EGR Solonoid Hose||||1||
Z||000000||grinthock||08-20-2001||05:01 PM||||There is a rubber hose that I found snipped on my EGR Solonoid, it comes out of the firewall side of the solonoid centre...  Where is this supposed to go?||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||08-20-2001||05:20 PM||||It goes to where there's clean air!  It normally (on V6 Fieros) goes to a metal tube attached to the firewall, the other end of which goes (via hose) to the "clean" side of the air filter (remember, that's the <B>outside</B> of the air filter element).<P>What does it do?  It's the vent for the EGR vacuum system.  It wants <B>clean</B> (filtered) air  there.  BTW, you're not alone - that hose often comes off, I suspect due to engine movement.  Might want to provide a little longer hose... but restrain it so it can't fall into the belts or anything!  Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">    ||||reg||1
